{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>But Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh remained alive of those men, etc.</b> This whole verse is superfluous — it is obvious that they lived, since they were not among those who brought back an evil report. Rather, it alludes to the statement of our Sages, of blessed memory (Hagigah 15a), that the righteous person receives his own portion and the portion of the wicked in Gan Eden. So too Joshua and Caleb received their own portions and the portions of the men who went with them to spy. And this is ״חָיוּ מִן הָאֲנָשִׁים״ — that they also received the portion of those men who went with them."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:13.827051719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}